TRODUTO' are crucial technical parameters that dictate the maximum percentage a cable duct or conduit can be filled with cables. These rates, typically set between 30-60% for channels and 40% for conduits, are essential for ensuring sufficient space for cable pulling during installation, preventing damage to cables, allowing for expansion, and facilitating ventilation. Adhering to these fill rates is vital for safe and effective electrical installations, directly impacting the integrity and longevity of the cabling system. [Data: Entities (2087, 2088), Relationships (2841, 2845, 2859,+more)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Variety of Cable Routing Systems under ROTA PERIMETRAL\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The ROTA PERIMETRAL concept is implemented through several specific types of routing systems. These include 'PERFIL DE PVC,' which may serve as a baseboard or crown molding with cable compartments; 'DUTO EMBUTIDO,' a concealed conduit; 'DUTO TIPO MOLDURA,' a molding-type duct also suitable for baseboards or crown moldings; and 'DUTO MULTICANAL,' a multi-channel duct system. Each of these provides a method for managing cables along perimeters, demonstrating the versatility and adaptability of the ROTA PERIMETRAL framework to different installation requirements and aesthetic considerations. [Data: Entities (2086, 2103, 2104, 2105, 2106), Relationships (2863, 2864, 2865, 2866,+more)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Distinction between Open and Closed Cable Routing in Handling\",\n            \"explanation\": \"A key distinction exists in cable handling between open systems like 'CANALETA APARENTE' and closed systems like 'ELETRODUTOS'. 'Canaletas aparentes' (apparent channels), particularly those installed as baseboards with dividers, allow for easier accommodation and manual handling of cables due to their open nature. Conversely, closed conduits, such as the 'CONDUTTE FLEXÍVEL LARANJA' (orange flexible conduit), do not